meta {
  name: Post GPS position
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/gps
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  DeviceId: {{deviceId}}
  Stream-Id: 1A2B3C4D
}

body:json {
  {
    "lat": 39.92,
    "lon": 9.65,
    "speed": 5.2,
    "course": 180.0,
    "altitude": 12.3,
    "sats": 9,
    "username": "{{username}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Stream-Id (optional, todo 67): the device's random per-boot stream id. Stored on
  the point (`gps_points.stream`) and returned by GET /gps, so the map splits a
  boat's day into streams EXACTLY instead of inferring a break from gaps. The
  firmware sends it on every POST /gps; a request without it stores NULL and the
  frontend falls back to the gap / impossible-speed / parked heuristics.
}
